     "id": "e2f3d9a3-adf7-497c-b5f3-23d7e0adad98"
    }
   ],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### 1.4 Worked Kramers-Kronig example for the SI\nA worked example of the Kramers-Kronig check exactly as it was run in 1.1 to 1.3, laid out for the SI so it can be repeated. Nothing is refitted with different settings; this section only re-plots and exports those results.\n\n**Procedure (as run).**\n1. Every spectrum of the 24 h drift run (458 spectra, Electrodes B1 to B3, 51 frequencies from 0.1 Hz to 10 kHz) is fitted with a linearized Kramers-Kronig model in admittance space, Y_KK(ω) = Y∞ + Σ_μ g_μ · iωτ_μ / (1 + iωτ_μ). There are M = 51 elements (one per measured frequency), with τ_μ spaced evenly in log τ from 1/(2π · 10 kHz) to 1/(2π · 0.1 Hz). Each term is Kramers-Kronig consistent by construction. The coefficients come from ordinary (unweighted) linear least squares on the stacked real and imaginary parts of Y, with no sign constraint.\n2. The residuals at each frequency are ΔRe = (Re Y − Re Y_KK)/|Y| and ΔIm = (Im Y − Im Y_KK)/|Y|.\n3. For each spectrum, the valid range is the longest run of consecutive frequencies where both residuals stay below 2%. Its lower end is that spectrum's fMin.\n4. fMinHz is the median of these lower ends over all 458 spectra. The upper cutoff fMaxHz is set separately, in 2.3.\n\n**What you see below.** Cell 17 prints a one-line summary and writes the CSVs. Cell 18 is the SI figure: (a) |Z| and (b) phase of the representative spectrum from 1.1, measured points with the Kramers-Kronig fit on top; (c) its residuals, with the ±2% lines and its valid range shaded; (d) the lower end of the valid range for all 458 drift spectra, with the median (fMinHz) dashed. Cell 19 tabulates the example and the percentiles that give fMinHz.\n\n**Files for replication** (`data/SI/`): the example spectrum with its fit and residuals (`kk_example_spectrum.csv`), its fitted coefficients (`kk_example_coefficients.csv`), and the residuals and valid range of every drift spectrum (`kk_drift_all_spectra.csv`).",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* 1.4  SI example of the Kramers-Kronig check exactly as run in 1.1 to 1.3: DCTKKCheck`KKCheck on\n   every drift spectrum, the 2 % valid-range rule, and fMinHz as the median lower bound. Nothing\n   is refitted with other settings. The coefficients are recomputed with the same code as\n   KKCheck only so they can be exported, and are checked against KKCheck's own fit.\n   Only kkSI* names are defined; fMinHz, kkAllResults and kkMins are read, never changed. *)\n\nkkSIDir  = FileNameJoin[{dctRoot, \"data\", \"SI\"}];\nkkSIFile = repFile;   kkSIRes = kkRep;          (* representative drift spectrum from 1.1 *)\n(* stop here, with a clear message, if Sections 1.1 to 1.3 have not run in this kernel *)\nIf[!(ListQ[kkMins] && AssociationQ[kkRep]),\n  Print[Style[\"1.4 needs the Section 1.1 to 1.3 results (kkAllResults, kkMins, kkRep): run those cells first.\", Darker[Red], Bold]];\n  Abort[]];\nkkSIName = DCTPlots`ElectrodeName[electrodeOf[kkSIFile]] <> \", drift spectrum \" <>\n  First[StringCases[FileBaseName[kkSIFile], \"(\" ~~ n : DigitCharacter .. ~~ \")\" :> n], FileBaseName[kkSIFile]];\n\n(* the fit behind KKCheck, repeated to expose its coefficients: admittance-space Maxwell basis,\n   M = number of frequencies, tau log-spaced over 1/(2 pi f), unweighted least squares on [Re Y; Im Y] *)\nkkSICoeffs[res_] := Module[{f = res[\"FreqHz\"], y = 1./res[\"Z\"], m = res[\"M\"], taus, wt, are, aim, th},\n  taus = 10.^Subdivide[Log10[1./(2. Pi Max[f])], Log10[1./(2. Pi Min[f])], m - 1];\n  wt   = Outer[Times, 2. Pi f, taus];\n  are  = Join[ConstantArray[1., {Length[f], 1}], wt^2/(1. + wt^2), 2];\n  aim  = Join[ConstantArray[0., {Length[f], 1}], wt/(1. + wt^2), 2];\n  th   = LeastSquares[Join[are, aim], Join[Re[y], Im[y]]];\n  <|\"Taus\" -> taus, \"YInf\" -> First[th], \"G\" -> Rest[th], \"ZFit\" -> 1./(are . th + I aim . th)|>];\nkkSICoef  = kkSICoeffs[kkSIRes];\nkkSIAgree = Max[Abs[kkSICoef[\"ZFit\"] - kkSIRes[\"ZFit\"]]/Abs[kkSIRes[\"ZFit\"]]];   (* should be ~1e-15 *)\n\nkkSIRange  = DCTKKCheck`KKValidFreqRange[kkSIRes, kkResidualThreshold];          (* this spectrum *)\nkkSIRanges = DCTKKCheck`KKValidFreqRange[#, kkResidualThreshold] & /@ kkAllResults; (* every spectrum *)\n\n(* ---- figure: (a) |Z|, (b) phase, (c) residuals + valid range, (d) fMin over all spectra ---- *)\nkkSIReady[] := ListQ[kkMins] && AssociationQ[kkSIRes];   (* Section 1.1 to 1.3 must have run *)\nkkSINotReady = Style[\"1.4 needs the Section 1.1 to 1.3 results (kkAllResults, kkMins, kkRep): run those cells first.\", Darker[Red], Bold];\n\nkkSIFigure[] := If[kkSIReady[], kkSIFigureImpl[], kkSINotReady];\nkkSIFigureImpl[] := Module[{fg, bg, r = kkSIRes, f, z, zf, fLo, fHi, ptCol, fitCol, reCol, imCol, bandCol, chrome,\n    zLo, zHi, pA, pB, pC, pD, resMax, tally, hLo, hHi, leg, dashed},\n  fg = If[DCTPlots`$DCTTheme === \"Publication\", Black, White];\n  bg = If[DCTPlots`$DCTTheme === \"Publication\", White, GrayLevel[0.12]];\n  ptCol   = If[DCTPlots`$DCTTheme === \"Publication\", GrayLevel[0.35], GrayLevel[0.8]];\n  bandCol = If[DCTPlots`$DCTTheme === \"Publication\", GrayLevel[0.92], GrayLevel[0.22]];\n  fitCol = RGBColor[0.85, 0.2, 0.15];\n  reCol  = RGBColor[0.2, 0.55, 0.95]; imCol = RGBColor[1., 0.6, 0.1];\n  dashed = Directive[fg, Opacity[0.5], AbsoluteDashing[{4, 3}], AbsoluteThickness[1.]];\n  f = r[\"FreqHz\"]; z = r[\"Z\"]; zf = r[\"ZFit\"]; {fLo, fHi} = MinMax[f];\n  chrome[xT_, yT_, xl_, yl_, ttl_, pr_] := Sequence[PlotTheme -> \"Default\", Frame -> True, Axes -> False,\n    Background -> bg, FrameStyle -> Directive[fg, AbsoluteThickness[1.1]], FrameTicks -> {{yT, None}, {xT, None}},\n    FrameTicksStyle -> Directive[fg, 11], LabelStyle -> Directive[fg, 12, FontFamily -> \"Arial\"],\n    FrameLabel -> {Style[xl, 12, fg], Style[yl, 12, fg]}, PlotLabel -> Style[ttl, 12, Bold, fg],\n    PlotRange -> pr, PlotRangePadding -> {Scaled[0.03], Scaled[0.05]}, ImageSize -> 360, AspectRatio -> 0.72];\n  {zLo, zHi} = MinMax[Abs[Join[z, zf]]];\n  pA = ListLogLogPlot[{Transpose[{f, Abs[zf]}], Transpose[{f, Abs[z]}]},\n    Joined -> {True, False}, PlotMarkers -> None,\n    PlotStyle -> {Directive[fitCol, AbsoluteThickness[1.6]], Directive[ptCol, PointSize[0.018]]},\n    chrome[DCTPlots`ThemeLogTicks[fLo, fHi, fg], DCTPlots`ThemeLogTicks[zLo, zHi, fg],\n      \"Frequency (Hz)\", \"|Z| (\\[CapitalOmega])\", \"(a) Modulus\", {{fLo, fHi}, {zLo, zHi}}]];\n  pB = ListLogLinearPlot[{Transpose[{f, -(180./Pi) Arg[zf]}], Transpose[{f, -(180./Pi) Arg[z]}]},\n    Joined -> {True, False}, PlotMarkers -> None,\n    PlotStyle -> {Directive[fitCol, AbsoluteThickness[1.6]], Directive[ptCol, PointSize[0.018]]},\n    chrome[DCTPlots`ThemeLogTicks[fLo, fHi, fg], DCTPlots`ThemeLinTicks[0., 90., fg],\n      \"Frequency (Hz)\", \"\\[Minus]phase of Z (\\[Degree])\", \"(b) Phase\", {{fLo, fHi}, {0., 90.}}]];\n  resMax = Max[1.5 100 kkResidualThreshold, 1.15 100 Max[Abs[Join[r[\"YResRe\"], r[\"YResIm\"]]]]];\n  (* shaded = this spectrum's valid range; log plots use NATURAL log coordinates internally *)\n  pC = ListLogLinearPlot[{Transpose[{f, 100 r[\"YResRe\"]}], Transpose[{f, 100 r[\"YResIm\"]}],\n      {{fLo, 100 kkResidualThreshold}, {fHi, 100 kkResidualThreshold}}, {{fLo, -100 kkResidualThreshold}, {fHi, -100 kkResidualThreshold}}},\n    Joined -> True, PlotMarkers -> {{\"\\[FilledCircle]\", 7}, {\"\\[FilledCircle]\", 7}, None, None},\n    PlotStyle -> {Directive[reCol, AbsoluteThickness[1.]], Directive[imCol, AbsoluteThickness[1.]], dashed, dashed},\n    Prolog -> {bandCol, Rectangle[{Log[kkSIRange[[1]]], -2 resMax}, {Log[kkSIRange[[2]]], 2 resMax}]},\n    GridLines -> {None, {0}}, GridLinesStyle -> Directive[fg, Opacity[0.25]],\n    chrome[DCTPlots`ThemeLogTicks[fLo, fHi, fg], DCTPlots`ThemeLinTicks[-resMax, resMax, fg],\n      \"Frequency (Hz)\", \"Residual (% of |Y|)\", \"(c) Residuals; shaded = valid range\", {{fLo, fHi}, {-resMax, resMax}}]];\n  (* per-spectrum lower bounds sit on the measured frequency grid, so count them per grid value *)\n  tally = SortBy[Tally[kkMins], First];\n  {hLo, hHi} = MinMax[tally[[All, 1]]] {1/1.6, 1.6};\n  pD = ListLogLinearPlot[{tally, {{fMinHz, 0}, {fMinHz, 1.1 Max[tally[[All, 2]]]}}},\n    Joined -> {False, True}, PlotMarkers -> None, Filling -> {1 -> Axis},\n    FillingStyle -> Directive[fitCol, AbsoluteThickness[6], Opacity[0.85]],\n    PlotStyle -> {Directive[fitCol, PointSize[0.001]], Directive[fg, AbsoluteDashing[{4, 3}], AbsoluteThickness[1.3]]},\n    chrome[DCTPlots`ThemeLogTicks[hLo, hHi, fg], DCTPlots`ThemeLinTicks[0., 1.1 Max[tally[[All, 2]]], fg],\n      \"Lower end of valid range (Hz)\", \"Drift spectra\",\n      \"(d) All \" <> ToString[Length[kkMins]] <> \" drift spectra\", {{hLo, hHi}, {0., 1.1 Max[tally[[All, 2]]]}}]];\n  leg = Row[{Graphics[{ptCol, PointSize[Large], Point[{0, 0}]}, ImageSize -> 10], \" measured   \",\n    Graphics[{fitCol, AbsoluteThickness[2], Line[{{0, 0}, {1, 0}}]}, ImageSize -> {26, 8}, PlotRange -> {{0, 1}, {-1, 1}}, AspectRatio -> 0.3], \" Kramers-Kronig fit   \",\n    Graphics[{reCol, AbsoluteThickness[2], Line[{{0, 0}, {1, 0}}]}, ImageSize -> {26, 8}, PlotRange -> {{0, 1}, {-1, 1}}, AspectRatio -> 0.3], \" \\[CapitalDelta]Re(Y)/|Y|   \",\n    Graphics[{imCol, AbsoluteThickness[2], Line[{{0, 0}, {1, 0}}]}, ImageSize -> {26, 8}, PlotRange -> {{0, 1}, {-1, 1}}, AspectRatio -> 0.3], \" \\[CapitalDelta]Im(Y)/|Y|   \",\n    Graphics[{dashed, Line[{{0, 0}, {1, 0}}]}, ImageSize -> {26, 8}, PlotRange -> {{0, 1}, {-1, 1}}, AspectRatio -> 0.3],\n    \" \\[PlusMinus]\" <> ToString[Round[100 kkResidualThreshold]] <> \"% threshold;  in (d), fMinHz = median = \" <> ToString[NumberForm[fMinHz, {3, 2}]] <> \" Hz\"},\n    BaseStyle -> {fg, 11, FontFamily -> \"Arial\"}];\n  Column[{Style[kkSIName <> \": linearized Kramers-Kronig check\", 13, Bold, fg],\n    Grid[{{pA, pB}, {pC, pD}}, Spacings -> {0.8, 0.8}], leg}, Alignment -> Center, Spacings -> 0.8,\n    Background -> bg]];\n\n(* ---- tables: the example spectrum, and the fMin distribution that sets fMinHz ---- *)\nkkSITables[] := If[kkSIReady[], kkSITablesImpl[], kkSINotReady];\nkkSITablesImpl[] := Module[{fg, r = kkSIRes, pct, hz, hdr, t1, t2},\n  fg = If[DCTPlots`$DCTTheme === \"Publication\", Black, White];\n  pct[x_] := ToString[NumberForm[100. x, {3, 2}]] <> \" %\";\n  hz[x_]  := ToString[NumberForm[x, {5, 3}]] <> \" Hz\";\n  hdr[l_] := Style[#, Bold, fg] & /@ l;\n  t1 = Grid[{hdr[{\"Example spectrum\", kkSIName}],\n      {\"frequencies\", ToString[Length[r[\"FreqHz\"]]] <> \", \" <> ToString[Min[r[\"FreqHz\"]]] <> \" to \" <> ToString[Round[Max[r[\"FreqHz\"]]]] <> \" Hz\"},\n      {\"Kramers-Kronig elements M\", ToString[r[\"M\"]] <> \" (one per measured frequency)\"},\n      {\"\\[Tau] range\", ToString[NumberForm[1*^6 Min[kkSICoef[\"Taus\"]], 3]] <> \" \\[Mu]s to \" <> ToString[NumberForm[Max[kkSICoef[\"Taus\"]], 3]] <> \" s\"},\n      {\"RMS residual, Re / Im\", pct[r[\"RMSRe\"]] <> \" / \" <> pct[r[\"RMSIm\"]]},\n      {\"valid range (both residuals < \" <> ToString[Round[100 kkResidualThreshold]] <> \" %)\", hz[kkSIRange[[1]]] <> \" to \" <> hz[kkSIRange[[2]]]}},\n    Frame -> All, FrameStyle -> GrayLevel[0.5], Alignment -> Left, Spacings -> {1.2, 0.6}, BaseStyle -> {fg, 12, FontFamily -> \"Arial\"}];\n  t2 = Grid[Join[{hdr[{\"Lower end of valid range, \" <> ToString[Length[kkMins]] <> \" drift spectra\", \"\"}]},\n      {ToString[#] <> \"th percentile\", hz[Quantile[kkMins, #/100.]]} & /@ {0, 25, 50, 75, 90, 100},\n      {{Style[\"fMinHz (\" <> ToString[kkFMinPercentile] <> \"th percentile)\", Bold, fg], Style[hz[fMinHz], Bold, fg]}}],\n    Frame -> All, FrameStyle -> GrayLevel[0.5], Alignment -> {{Left, Right}}, Spacings -> {1.2, 0.6}, BaseStyle -> {fg, 12, FontFamily -> \"Arial\"}];\n  Column[{t1, t2}, Spacings -> 1.2]];\n\n(* ---- replication files in data/SI ---- *)\nIf[!DirectoryQ[kkSIDir], CreateDirectory[kkSIDir]];\nExport[FileNameJoin[{kkSIDir, \"kk_example_spectrum.csv\"}],\n  Prepend[Transpose[{kkSIRes[\"FreqHz\"], Re[kkSIRes[\"Z\"]], Im[kkSIRes[\"Z\"]], Re[kkSIRes[\"ZFit\"]], Im[kkSIRes[\"ZFit\"]],\n      kkSIRes[\"YResRe\"], kkSIRes[\"YResIm\"]}],\n    {\"f_Hz\", \"Zre_ohm\", \"Zim_ohm\", \"ZKKre_ohm\", \"ZKKim_ohm\", \"resRe_frac_of_absY\", \"resIm_frac_of_absY\"}], \"CSV\"];\nExport[FileNameJoin[{kkSIDir, \"kk_example_coefficients.csv\"}],\n  Join[{{\"term\", \"tau_s\", \"value_S\"}, {\"Y_inf\", \"\", kkSICoef[\"YInf\"]}},\n    MapThread[{\"g\" <> ToString[#1], #2, #3} &, {Range[Length[kkSICoef[\"G\"]]], kkSICoef[\"Taus\"], kkSICoef[\"G\"]}]], \"CSV\"];\nExport[FileNameJoin[{kkSIDir, \"kk_drift_all_spectra.csv\"}],\n  Prepend[MapThread[{DCTPlots`ElectrodeName[electrodeOf[#1]], FileNameTake[#1], #2[\"RMSRe\"], #2[\"RMSIm\"], #3[[1]], #3[[2]]} &,\n      {driftFiles, kkAllResults, kkSIRanges}],\n    {\"electrode\", \"file\", \"RMS_resRe\", \"RMS_resIm\", \"valid_fmin_Hz\", \"valid_fmax_Hz\"}], \"CSV\"];\n\nPrint[kkSIName, \": RMS residual \", NumberForm[100 kkSIRes[\"RMSRe\"], {3, 2}], \" % (Re), \",\n  NumberForm[100 kkSIRes[\"RMSIm\"], {3, 2}], \" % (Im); valid \", kkSIRange[[1]], \" to \", kkSIRange[[2]], \" Hz.  \",\n  \"fMinHz = median over \", Length[kkMins], \" spectra = \", NumberForm[fMinHz, {4, 3}], \" Hz.  \",\n  \"Coefficient check vs KKCheck: \", ScientificForm[kkSIAgree, 2], \".  CSVs in \", kkSIDir];",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
       "data": "<div class=\"wl-print-output\"><div class=\"wl-print-line\"><span class=\"wl-ps\">Electrode B1, drift spectrum 0</span><span class=\"wl-ps\">: RMS residual </span><div class=\"vscode-wolfram-wllatex-prerendered\" data-page-width-em=\"64\" data-latex-b64=\"XHRleHR7MS4yNn0=\"><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">1.26</span></span></span></span></span></span></div><span class=\"wl-ps\"> % (Re), </span><div class=\"vscode-wolfram-wllatex-prerendered\" data-page-width-em=\"64\" data-latex-b64=\"XHRleHR7MC44Mn0=\"><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">0.82</span></span></span></span></span></span></div><span class=\"wl-ps\"> % (Im); valid </span><div class=\"vscode-wolfram-wllatex-prerendered\" data-page-width-em=\"64\" data-latex-b64=\"MC43OTQzMw==\"><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">0.79433</span></span></span></span></span></div><span class=\"wl-ps\"> to </span><div class=\"vscode-wolfram-wllatex-prerendered\" data-page-width-em=\"64\" data-latex-b64=\"MTAwMDA=\"><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">10000</span></span></span></span></span></div><span class=\"wl-ps\"> Hz.  </span><span class=\"wl-ps\">fMinHz = median over </span><div class=\"vscode-wolfram-wllatex-prerendered\" data-page-width-em=\"64\" data-latex-b64=\"NDU4\"><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">458</span></span></span></span></span></div><span class=\"wl-ps\"> spectra = </span><div class=\"vscode-wolfram-wllatex-prerendered\" data-page-width-em=\"64\" data-latex-b64=\"XHRleHR7Mi41MTJ9\"><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">2.512</span></span></span></span></span></span></div><span class=\"wl-ps\"> Hz.  </span><span class=\"wl-ps\">Coefficient check vs KKCheck: </span><div class=\"vscode-wolfram-wllatex-prerendered\" data-page-width-em=\"64\" data-latex-b64=\"XHRleHR7MC59\"><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">0.</span></span></span></span></span></span></div><span class=\"wl-ps\">.  CSVs in </span><span class=\"wl-ps\">c:\\\\Users\\\\Bob Lansdorp\\\\Documents\\\\DCT\\\\data\\\\SI</span></div></div>",
       "mime": "x-application/wolfram-language-html"
