  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### 4a.6 k-range definitions",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* k windows for the two electron-transfer populations. The slow/fast boundary is NOT\n   hardcoded and NOT global: every spectrum is split at the centre of its OWN zero gap\n   between the two peaks (peakWindows), found by valleyK seeded at 100 /s. The gap moves\n   with concentration (about 73 /s at 1000 uM, 116 /s at 0 uM), so a per-spectrum boundary\n   follows the physics instead of clipping one tail or the other. The outer edges, 10 and\n   500 /s, bracket the fitted band; the sensitivity analysis (7.6) showed them irrelevant. *)\n\n(* valley between the two peaks. The slow peak is the tallest LOCAL MAXIMUM below kGuess and\n   the fast peak the tallest local maximum above it. Local maxima, not merely the tallest\n   points: when one population is nearly gone (e.g. the unweighted fit at high [target]),\n   the other peak's flank can be taller than the small peak on the wrong side of kGuess,\n   and taking the tallest point would land on that flank. Between the two peaks the\n   regularised NNLS solution has a flat floor of (near) zeros rather than a single minimum,\n   so the boundary is the geometric centre of that floor: every point within 2% of the\n   smaller peak height above the minimum. Returns kGuess if either peak is missing. *)\nvalleyK[k_List, g_List, kGuess_] := Module[{o, ks, gs, n, maxima, lo, hi, pLo, pHi, seg, tol, floor},\n  o = Ordering[k]; ks = k[[o]]; gs = g[[o]]; n = Length[gs];\n  maxima = Select[Range[2, n - 1], gs[[#]] > gs[[# - 1]] && gs[[#]] >= gs[[# + 1]] &];\n  lo = Select[maxima, ks[[#]] < kGuess &];\n  hi = Select[maxima, ks[[#]] > kGuess &];\n  If[lo === {} && hi === {}, Return[N[kGuess]]];\n  (* one population absent: put the boundary at the edge of the surviving peak's support\n     (where g falls to 2% of that peak), so the empty window holds only the zero floor and\n     never a sliver of the other peak's flank *)\n  If[lo === {}, pHi = hi[[First @ Ordering[gs[[hi]], -1]]];\n    floor = Select[Range[1, pHi], gs[[#]] <= 0.02 gs[[pHi]] &];\n    Return[If[floor === {}, N[kGuess], ks[[Max[floor]]]]]];\n  If[hi === {}, pLo = lo[[First @ Ordering[gs[[lo]], -1]]];\n    floor = Select[Range[pLo, n], gs[[#]] <= 0.02 gs[[pLo]] &];\n    Return[If[floor === {}, N[kGuess], ks[[Min[floor]]]]]];\n  pLo = lo[[First @ Ordering[gs[[lo]], -1]]];\n  pHi = hi[[First @ Ordering[gs[[hi]], -1]]];\n  seg   = Range[pLo, pHi];\n  tol   = Min[gs[[seg]]] + 0.02 Min[gs[[pLo]], gs[[pHi]]];\n  floor = Select[seg, gs[[#]] <= tol &];\n  Exp[Mean[Log[ks[[floor]]]]]];\n\nkSplitGuess = 100.;\n\n(* per-spectrum windows: {slow, fast}, split at the centre of that spectrum's own gap *)\npeakWindows[spec_] := With[{v = valleyK[1./spec[\"Tau\"], spec[\"g\"], kSplitGuess]}, {{10., v}, {v, 500.}}];\n\n(* fixed windows at the seed, kept only for the package k-peak tracker in 4a.7, which takes\n   fixed ranges. Every folded-fraction and rate calculation in this notebook uses peakWindows. *)\nkPeakRanges = {{10., kSplitGuess}, {kSplitGuess, 500.}};\n\n(* diagnostics: where the gap sits in the drift run *)\ndriftK      = 1./goodSpecs[[1]][\"Spec\"][\"Tau\"];               (* all drift fits share one tau grid *)\ndriftGMean  = Mean[#Spec[\"g\"] & /@ goodSpecs];\nkSplit      = valleyK[driftK, driftGMean, kSplitGuess];\nkSplitPer   = valleyK[1./#Spec[\"Tau\"], #Spec[\"g\"], kSplitGuess] & /@ goodSpecs;\nPrint[Style[\"Drift run gap centre, mean g(k): \", Bold], NumberForm[kSplit, {4, 1}], \" /s\",\n  \"   (per-spectrum: median \", NumberForm[Median[kSplitPer], {4, 1}],\n  \", 5th to 95th percentile \", NumberForm[Quantile[kSplitPer, 0.05], {4, 1}], \" to \",\n  NumberForm[Quantile[kSplitPer, 0.95], {4, 1}], \" /s)\"];\n\nDCTPlots`PlotGK[{<|\"File\" -> \"mean of \" <> ToString[Length[goodSpecs]] <> \" drift spectra\",\n    \"Spec\" -> <|\"Tau\" -> goodSpecs[[1]][\"Spec\"][\"Tau\"], \"g\" -> driftGMean|>|>},\n  Automatic, \"GScale\" -> 1*^9, ImageSize -> 560, PlotLegends -> None,\n  GridLines -> {{{kSplit, Directive[Orange, Dashed, AbsoluteThickness[1.5]]},\n                 {10., Directive[Gray, Dotted]}, {500., Directive[Gray, Dotted]}}, None},\n  PlotLabel -> Style[\"Mean drift g(k) with the detected slow/fast boundary\", 13, Bold]]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
       "data": "<div class=\"wl-print-output\"><div class=\"wl-print-line\"><div class=\"vscode-wolfram-wllatex-prerendered\" data-page-width-em=\"64\" data-latex-b64=\"XG1hdGhiZntcdGV4dHtEcmlmdCBydW4gZ2FwIGNlbnRyZSwgbWVhbiBnKGspOiB9fQ==\"><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">Drift run gap centre, mean g(k): </span></span></span></span></span></span></div><div class=\"vscode-wolfram-wllatex-prerendered\" data-page-width-em=\"64\" data-latex-b64=\"XHRleHR7NzkuMX0=\"><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">79.1</span></span></span></span></span></span></div><span class=\"wl-ps\"> /s</span><span class=\"wl-ps\">   (per-spectrum: median </span><div class=\"vscode-wolfram-wllatex-prerendered\" data-page-width-em=\"64\" data-latex-b64=\"XHRleHR7NzkuMX0=\"><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">79.1</span></span></span></span></span></span></div><span class=\"wl-ps\">, 5th to 95th percentile </span><div class=\"vscode-wolfram-wllatex-prerendered\" data-page-width-em=\"64\" data-latex-b64=\"XHRleHR7NzkuMX0=\"><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">79.1</span></span></span></span></span></span></div><span class=\"wl-ps\"> to </span><div class=\"vscode-wolfram-wllatex-prerendered\" data-page-width-em=\"64\" data-latex-b64=\"XHRleHR7ODUuNH0=\"><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">85.4</span></span></span></span></span></span></div><span class=\"wl-ps\"> /s)</span></div></div>",
       "mime": "x-application/wolfram-language-html"
      },
      {
       "data": "Print: [formula][formula] /s   (per-spectrum: median[formula], 5th to 95th percentile[formula] to[formula] /s)",
       "mime": "text/plain"
      }
     ],
     "id": "99e53f94-1c56-4d6a-bf62-9bbaf549c329"
    },
    {
     "items": [
      {
       "data": "<div class=\"wl-output-block\"><div class=\"wl-output-header\" style=\"display:flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;width:100%;min-height:22px;\" data-session-epoch=\"23243\" data-output-id=\"46\" data-out-n=\"345\" data-sub-idx=\"14\" data-output-format=\"SVG\" data-output-is-graphics=\"1\" data-cell-idx=\"59\" data-sub-start=\"56\" data-sub-end=\"61\"><span style=\"font-size:10px;color:#888;margin-right:8px;\">Out[345]=</span></div><div class=\"wl-output-content\"><span class=\"vscode-wolfram-gfx-marker\" style=\"display:none;\"></span><img class=\"vscode-wolfram-svg-output\" data-wl-img=\"c:\\\\Users\\\\Bob Lansdorp\\\\Documents\\\\DCT\\\\img\\\\EAB_DCT_analysis\\\\wl_ttuuypduh2kz.svg\" width=\"747\" height=\"532\" src=\"img/EAB_DCT_analysis/wl_ttuuypduh2kz.svg\"/></div></div>",
       "mime": "x-application/wolfram-language-html"
      },
      {
       "data": "(* output: graphics *)\n(* k windows for the two electron-transfer populations. The slow/fast boundary is NOT\n   hardcoded and NOT global: every spectrum is split at the centre of its OWN zero gap\n   between the two peaks (peakWindows), found by valleyK seeded at 100 /s. The gap moves\n   with concentration (about 73 /s at 1000 uM, 116 /s at 0 uM), so a per-spectrum boundary\n   follows the physics instead of clipping one tail or the other. The outer edges, 10 and\n   500 /s, bracket the fitted band; the sensitivity analysis (7.6) showed them irrelevant. *)\n\n(* valley between the two peaks. The slow peak is the tallest LOCAL MAXIMUM below kGuess and\n   the fast peak the tallest local maximum above it. Local maxima, not merely the tallest\n   points: when one population is nearly gone (e.g. the unweighted fit at high [target]),\n   the other peak's flank can be taller than the small peak on the wrong side of kGuess,\n   and taking the tallest point would land on that flank. Between the two peaks the\n   regularised NNLS solution has a flat floor of (near) zeros rather than a single minimum,\n   so the boundary is the geometric centre of that floor: every point within 2% of the\n   smaller peak height above the minimum. Returns kGuess if either peak is missing. *)\nvalleyK[k_List, g_List, kGuess_] := Module[{o, ks, gs, n, maxima, lo, hi, pLo, pHi, seg, tol, floor},\n  o = Ordering[k]; ks = k[[o]]; gs = g[[o]]; n = Length[gs];\n  maxima = Select[Range[2, n - 1], gs[[#]] > gs[[# - 1]] && gs[[#]] >= gs[[# + 1]] &];\n  lo = Select[maxima, ks[[#]] < kGuess &];\n  hi = Select[maxima, ks[[#]] > kGuess &];\n  If[lo === {} && hi === {}, Return[N[kGuess]]];\n  (* one population absent: put the boundary at the edge of the surviving peak's support\n     (where g falls to 2% of that peak), so the empty window holds only the zero floor and\n     never a sliver of the other peak's flank *)\n  If[lo === {}, pHi = hi[[First @ Ordering[gs[[hi]], -1]]];\n    floor = Select[Range[1, pHi], gs[[#]] <= 0.02 gs[[pHi]] &];\n    Return[If[floor === {}, N[kGuess], ks[[Max[floor]]]]]];\n  If[hi === {}, pLo = lo[[First @ Ordering[gs[[lo]], -1]]];\n    floor = Select[Range[pLo, n], gs[[#]] <= 0.02 gs[[pLo]] &];\n    Return[If[floor === {}, N[kGuess], ks[[Min[floor]]]]]];\n  pLo = lo[[First @ Ordering[gs[[lo]], -1]]];\n  pHi = hi[[First @ Ordering[gs[[hi]], -1]]];\n  seg   = Range[pLo, pHi];\n  tol   = Min[gs[[seg]]] + 0.02 Min[gs[[pLo]], gs[[pHi]]];\n  floor = Select[seg, gs[[#]] <= tol &];\n  Exp[Mean[Log[ks[[floor]]]]]];\n\nkSplitGuess = 100.;\n\n(* per-spectrum windows: {slow, fast}, split at the centre of that spectrum's own gap *)\npeakWindows[spec_] := With[{v = valleyK[1./spec[\"Tau\"], spec[\"g\"], kSplitGuess]}, {{10., v}, {v, 500.}}];\n\n(* fixed windows at the seed, kept only for the package k-peak tracker in 4a.7, which takes\n   fixed ranges. Every folded-fraction and rate calculation in this notebook uses peakWindows. *)\nkPeakRanges = {{10., kSplitGuess}, {kSplitGuess, 500.}};\n\n(* diagnostics: where the gap sits in the drift run *)\ndriftK      = 1./goodSpecs[[1]][\"Spec\"][\"Tau\"];               (* all drift fits share one tau grid *)\ndriftGMean  = Mean[#Spec[\"g\"] & /@ goodSpecs];\nkSplit      = valleyK[driftK, driftGMean, kSplitGuess];\nkSplitPer   = valleyK[1./#Spec[\"Tau\"], #Spec[\"g\"], kSplitGuess] & /@ goodSpecs;\nPrint[Style[\"Drift run gap centre, mean g(k): \", Bold], NumberForm[kSplit, {4, 1}], \" /s\",\n  \"   (per-spectrum: median \", NumberForm[Median[kSplitPer], {4, 1}],\n  \", 5th to 95th percentile \", NumberForm[Quantile[kSplitPer, 0.05], {4, 1}], \" to \",\n  NumberForm[Quantile[kSplitPer, 0.95], {4, 1}], \" /s)\"];\n\nDCTPlots`PlotGK[{<|\"File\" -> \"mean of \" <> ToString[Length[goodSpecs]] <> \" drift spectra\",\n    \"Spec\" -> <|\"Tau\" -> goodSpecs[[1]][\"Spec\"][\"Tau\"], \"g\" -> driftGMean|>|>},\n  Automatic, \"GScale\" -> 1*^9, ImageSize -> 560, PlotLegends -> None,\n  GridLines -> {{{kSplit, Directive[Orange, Dashed, AbsoluteThickness[1.5]]},\n                 {10., Directive[Gray, Dotted]}, {500., Directive[Gray, Dotted]}}, None},\n  PlotLabel -> Style[\"Mean drift g(k) with the detected slow/fast boundary\", 13, Bold]]",
       "mime": "text/plain"
      }
