   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### 7.4 Per-state rates: sweeps with the spectra retained\nSame four sweeps as 7.2, but each refit is kept so the g-weighted geometric mean rate of the slow (unfolded, range 1) and fast (folded, range 2) populations can be pooled by concentration, exactly the quantity of section 5.5. Presented in 7.6.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* 7.4  Refit every sweep case again, this time RETAINING the spectra, then pool the\n   per-state mean rate <k> by concentration. windowGeoMean is the section 5.5 function. *)\n\nsensRecsCase[param_, xVal_, label_, fMin_, fMax_, lam_, wp_] :=\n  <|\"Param\" -> param, \"X\" -> xVal, \"Label\" -> label, \"Recs\" -> sensFitConc[fMin, fMax, lam, wp]|>;\n\n(* pooled {conc, <k>} curve for window wi (1 = slow, 2 = fast): mean over electrodes,\n   Missing entries dropped; each spectrum uses its own gap-centred window (peakWindows) *)\nrateCurve[recs_, wi_] := SortBy[KeyValueMap[{#1, Mean[#2]} &,\n  GroupBy[DeleteMissing[{#Conc, windowGeoMean[#Spec, Sequence @@ peakWindows[#Spec][[wi]]]} & /@ recs, 1, 2], First -> Last]], First];\n\nrateBase = sensRecsCase[\"baseline\", None, \"baseline\", fMinHz, fMaxHz, lambdaND, weightPower];\n\nrateCasesKK = Table[sensRecsCase[\"KK threshold\", t,\n    ToString[NumberForm[100 t, {3, 1}]] <> \"%  (fMin \" <> ToString[NumberForm[fMinOf[t], {4, 2}]] <> \" Hz)\",\n    fMinOf[t], fMaxHz, lambdaND, weightPower], {t, kkThresholds}];\nrateCasesWP = Table[sensRecsCase[\"weightPower\", wp, \"p = \" <> ToString[wp],\n    fMinHz, fMaxHz, lambdaND, wp], {wp, weightPowers}];\nrateCasesFM = Table[sensRecsCase[\"fMaxHz\", fm, ToString[NumberForm[fm, {5, 1}]] <> \" Hz\",\n    fMinHz, fm, lambdaND, weightPower], {fm, fMaxVals}];\nrateCasesLam = Table[sensRecsCase[\"lambdaND\", k lambdaND, ToString[k] <> \" x\",\n    fMinHz, fMaxHz, k lambdaND, weightPower], {k, lamFactors}];\n\nrateAll = <|\"KK threshold\" -> rateCasesKK, \"weightPower\" -> rateCasesWP,\n            \"fMaxHz\" -> rateCasesFM, \"lambdaND\" -> rateCasesLam|>;\nPrint[Style[\"Rate sweeps done: \" <> ToString[1 + Total[Length /@ Values[rateAll]]] <> \" refits kept.\", Bold, Darker[Green]]]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
       "data": "<div class=\"wl-print-output\"><div class=\"wl-print-line\"><div class=\"vscode-wolfram-wllatex-prerendered\" data-page-width-em=\"64\" data-latex-b64=\"XG1hdGhiZntcdGV4dGNvbG9yeyMwMGZmMDB9e1x0ZXh0e1JhdGUgc3dlZXBzIGRvbmU6IDIxIHJlZml0cyBrZXB0Ln19fQ==\"><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.8889em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord text\" style=\"color:#00ff00;\"><span class=\"mord\" style=\"color:#00ff00;\">Rate sweeps done: 21 refits kept.</span></span></span></span></span></span></div></div></div>",
       "mime": "x-application/wolfram-language-html"
      },
      {
       "data": "Print: [formula]",
       "mime": "text/plain"
      }
     ],
     "id": "dee24ea3-46c4-40ea-8fd9-bd5ee2a0adea"
    }
   ],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* 7.4b  The numbers behind the fast-mode capacitive fraction plot of 7.3, and the reason\n   the pooled p = 0 curve reaches ~1 while the Electrode B1 spectra above it plainly still\n   show a slow peak: the curve is a MEAN OVER ELECTRODES, and at p = 0 some electrodes\n   lose their slow population entirely, so their window split leaves an empty slow window\n   and ff = 1 exactly. Table A is what is plotted (pooled); table B is Electrode B1 alone,\n   which is what the spectra panels show. Each exponent gets two columns: the fast-mode\n   capacitive fraction and k_mid, the midpoint electron-transfer rate dividing the slow\n   and fast modes (the gap centre found per spectrum by peakWindows, 4a.6, in 1/s). *)\npCols    = {0., weightPower, -1.};                  (* column order = panel order of 7.3 *)\npColLbl  = {\"p = 0\", \"baseline\", \"p = -1\"};\nffCurveOfP[p_] := If[p == weightPower, ffRef, ffByP[p]];\nrecsOfP[p_]    := If[p == weightPower, rateBase[\"Recs\"], First[Select[rateCasesWP, #[\"X\"] == p &]][\"Recs\"]];\ne1SpecsOfP[p_] := If[p == weightPower, gkBase, gkByP[p]];\nkMid[spec_]      := peakWindows[spec][[1, 2]];\ndegenerateQ[ff_] := ff >= 0.999 || ff <= 0.001;   (* empty slow window, or empty fast window *)\n\nffAssocP  = Association[(# -> Association[Rule @@@ ffCurveOfP[#]]) & /@ pCols];\nconcList  = ffRef[[All, 1]];\n(* pooled midpoint rate: mean over the electrodes measured at that concentration *)\nkMidAssocP = Association[Table[p -> Association[Table[\n     c -> Mean[kMid[#Spec] & /@ Select[recsOfP[p], #Conc == c &]], {c, concList}]], {p, pCols}]];\nnAtConc   = Association[Table[c -> Length[Select[rateBase[\"Recs\"], #Conc == c &]], {c, concList}]];\ndegAtConc = Association[Table[\n   c -> Count[sensFF[#Spec] & /@ Select[recsOfP[0.], #Conc == c &], _?degenerateQ], {c, concList}]];\n\n(* two-level header: each exponent spans its ff and k_mid columns *)\nhdrPair = Flatten[Table[{Style[\"ff\", Bold], Style[\"k_mid (1/s)\", Bold]}, {Length[pCols]}], 1];\nspanLbl = Flatten[Table[{Style[l, Bold], SpanFromLeft}, {l, pColLbl}], 1];\n\ntableA = Grid[Join[\n   {Join[{\"\"}, spanLbl, {Style[\"n elec\", Bold], Style[\"degen.\", Bold]}]},\n   {Join[{Style[\"[Vanco] (\\[Mu]M)\", Bold]}, hdrPair, {\"\", \"at p = 0\"}]},\n   Table[Join[{NumberForm[c, {4, 0}]},\n     Flatten[Table[{NumberForm[ffAssocP[p][c], {4, 3}], NumberForm[kMidAssocP[p][c], {4, 1}]}, {p, pCols}], 1],\n     {nAtConc[c], If[degAtConc[c] > 0, degAtConc[c], \"n/a\"]}], {c, concList}]],\n  Frame -> All, Alignment -> {{Right}}, Spacings -> {1.1, 0.5},\n  BaseStyle -> {FontFamily -> \"Arial\", FontSize -> 10}];\n\n(* Electrode B1 only, the series drawn in the spectra panels *)\ne1Conc = Sort[N@getLabelUM[#File] & /@ gkBase];\ntableB = Grid[Join[\n   {Join[{\"\"}, spanLbl]},\n   {Join[{Style[\"[Vanco] (\\[Mu]M)\", Bold]}, hdrPair]},\n   Table[Join[{NumberForm[c, {4, 0}]},\n     Flatten[Table[Module[{s = First[Select[e1SpecsOfP[p], N@getLabelUM[#File] == c &]][\"Spec\"]},\n         {NumberForm[sensFF[s], {4, 3}], NumberForm[kMid[s], {4, 1}]}], {p, pCols}], 1]], {c, e1Conc}]],\n  Frame -> All, Alignment -> {{Right}}, Spacings -> {1.1, 0.5},\n  BaseStyle -> {FontFamily -> \"Arial\", FontSize -> 10}];\n\nPrint[Style[\"A. Fast-mode capacitive fraction and midpoint rate, pooled over electrodes (this is what 7.3 plots)\", Bold, 13]];\nPrint[tableA];\nPrint[Style[\"B. Electrode B1 only (the series shown in the spectra panels)\", Bold, 13]];\nPrint[tableB];\nPrint[Style[Row[{\"At p = 0, \", Count[sensFF[#Spec] & /@ recsOfP[0.], _?(# >= 0.999 &)],\n  \" of the 39 spectra come out at ff = 1 exactly (the unweighted fit has collapsed the slow population, so the slow window is empty) and \",\n  Count[sensFF[#Spec] & /@ recsOfP[0.], _?(# <= 0.001 &)],\n  \" at ff = 0 exactly (the detector put the split above the single surviving peak). Those are what push the pooled p = 0 curve to \",\n  NumberForm[Last[ffCurveOfP[0.]][[2]], {4, 3}], \" at 1000 \\[Mu]M while Electrode B1 alone is \",\n  NumberForm[sensFF[First[Select[gkByP[0.], N@getLabelUM[#File] == 1000. &]][\"Spec\"]], {4, 3}],\n  \". Neither the baseline nor p = -1 produces a degenerate spectrum. Note also that k_mid falls as the weighting is removed, so part of the slow peak's fast flank is counted as fast.\"}], Italic]]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
       "data": "<div class=\"wl-print-output\"><div class=\"wl-print-line\"><div class=\"vscode-wolfram-wllatex-prerendered\" data-page-width-em=\"65\" data-latex-b64=\"XG1hdGhiZntcdGV4dHtBLiBGYXN0LW1vZGUgY2FwYWNpdGl2ZSBmcmFjdGlvbiBhbmQgbWlkcG9pbnQgcmF0ZSwgcG9vbGVkIG92ZXIgZWxlY3Ryb2RlcyAodGhpcyBpcyB3aGF0IDcuMyBwbG90cyl9fQ==\"><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">A. Fast-mode capacitive fraction and midpoint rate, pooled over electrodes (this is what 7.3 plots)</span></span></span></span></span></span></div></div></div>",
       "mime": "x-application/wolfram-language-html"
      },
      {
       "data": "Print: [formula]",
       "mime": "text/plain"
      }
     ],
     "id": "75b7cdc9-4495-4a89-9329-8c407dfcdf73"
    },
    {
