    {
     "items": [
      {
       "data": "<div class=\"wl-output-block\"><div class=\"wl-output-header\" style=\"display:flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;width:100%;min-height:22px;\" data-session-epoch=\"23243\" data-output-id=\"67\" data-out-n=\"619\" data-sub-idx=\"5\" data-output-format=\"SVG\" data-output-is-graphics=\"1\" data-cell-idx=\"117\" data-sub-start=\"18\" data-sub-end=\"20\"><span style=\"font-size:10px;color:#888;margin-right:8px;\">Out[619]=</span></div><div class=\"wl-output-content\"><span class=\"vscode-wolfram-gfx-marker\" style=\"display:none;\"></span><img class=\"vscode-wolfram-svg-output\" data-wl-img=\"c:\\\\Users\\\\Bob Lansdorp\\\\Documents\\\\DCT\\\\img\\\\EAB_DCT_analysis\\\\wl_f5uhni9lf8s6.svg\" width=\"1105\" height=\"676\" src=\"img/EAB_DCT_analysis/wl_f5uhni9lf8s6.svg\"/></div></div>",
       "mime": "x-application/wolfram-language-html"
      },
      {
       "data": "(* output: graphics *)\n(* 7.7  Representative spectrum vs fMaxHz: Electrode B1 at 562 uM refit at each cutoff of the 7.2\n   sweep, all other parameters at baseline. Dashed line = the gap centre of the baseline\n   fit (effective cutoff fMaxEff), i.e. that spectrum's own slow/fast boundary from peakWindows.\n   Own variable name (repFileFMax): repFile belongs to section 1 and feeds the lambda sweep. *)\nrepFileFMax = First @ Select[FileNames[\"*.txt\", concentrationDir], concElec[#] == \"1\" && concUM[#] == 562 &];\nrepFMax = Table[<|\"File\" -> ToString[NumberForm[fm, {5, 1}]] <> \" Hz\",\n    \"Spec\" -> DCT`DCTSpectrum[repFileFMax, \"LambdaND\" -> lambdaND, \"FMinUse\" -> fMinHz, \"FMaxUse\" -> fm,\n      \"WeightPower\" -> weightPower, \"BinsPerDecade\" -> binsPerDecade,\n      \"TauMinFactor\" -> tauMinFactor, \"TauMaxFactor\" -> tauMaxFactor]|>, {fm, fMaxVals}];\n\n(* the numbers behind the picture *)\nPrint[Grid[Prepend[\n  Table[{c[\"File\"], NumberForm[peakWindows[c[\"Spec\"]][[1, 2]], {4, 1}], NumberForm[sensFF[c[\"Spec\"]], {4, 3}],\n         NumberForm[windowGeoMean[c[\"Spec\"], Sequence @@ peakWindows[c[\"Spec\"]][[1]]], {4, 1}],\n         NumberForm[windowGeoMean[c[\"Spec\"], Sequence @@ peakWindows[c[\"Spec\"]][[2]]], {4, 1}]}, {c, repFMax}],\n  Style[#, Bold] & /@ {\"fMaxHz\", \"gap centre (1/s)\", \"ff\", \"slow <k> (1/s)\", \"fast <k> (1/s)\"}],\n  Frame -> All, Alignment -> {{Left, Right, Right, Right, Right}}, Spacings -> {2, 0.6}]];\n\nDCTPlots`PlotGK[repFMax, Automatic, \"GScale\" -> 1*^9, ImageSize -> 720,\n  GridLines -> {{{peakWindows[repFMax[[First @ FirstPosition[fMaxVals, fMaxEff]]][\"Spec\"]][[1, 2]], Directive[Gray, Dashed]}}, None},\n  PlotLabel -> Style[\"Electrode B1, 562 \\[Mu]M:  g(k) vs upper frequency cutoff fMaxHz\", 14, Bold]]",
       "mime": "text/plain"
      }
     ],
     "id": "d680caa5-6db5-43f2-b796-a94f1d38b33f"
    }
   ],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## 8. Neglecting the solution resistance (Rs = 0)\nEvery fit so far optimises Rs in an outer Brent loop and inverts the interfacial admittance Y = 1/(Z - Rs). This section asks what the DCT spectrum looks like if the solution resistance is ignored, so that the whole measured impedance is attributed to the interface, Y = 1/Z. The inner solve is called directly (`DCTKernel`SolveLadderGivenRs` with Rs = 0), so the tau grid, the regularisation and the weighting are identical to the baseline and only the Rs subtraction is removed.\n\nThe short answer: the inversion does not fail, and it does not even fit the impedance worse, but it stops being interpretable. Roughly a third of the recovered capacitance moves to the fast edge of the tau grid, the two physical peaks broaden and shift, and the folded fraction is wrong by an amount that varies with concentration (0.086 to 0.010 at 0 µM, 0.63 to 0.82 at 1000 µM), which would change every biophysical parameter in section 5a.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### 8.1 Refit with Rs = 0 and compare, per concentration\nRs (fitted) is the value the baseline Brent loop chose, around 160 to 185 Ω here. The misfit is the relative impedance residual |Z_fit - Z_data| / |Z_data| over the fit band. Note that it goes DOWN at Rs = 0 (about 0.5% against 1.2 to 1.5% for the baseline): dropping Rs does not cost fit quality in this window, because the ladder can reproduce the missing series term with very fast relaxations. Goodness of fit in Z therefore does not discriminate between the two models; what discriminates is where the capacitance ends up, which is the last column.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* 8.1  Refit every concentration spectrum with the solution resistance held at zero.\n   DCTSpectrum optimises Rs, so the inner solve is called directly instead: the tau grid,\n   regularisation and weighting are the baseline ones, only the Rs subtraction is gone\n   (Y = 1/Z instead of Y = 1/(Z - Rs)). *)\nrsZeroSpec[file_] := Module[{dat, keep, fr, z},\n  dat = DCTDataImport`ImportEIS[file];\n  If[FailureQ[dat], Return[$Failed]];\n  keep = Select[Transpose[{dat[\"FreqHz\"], dat[\"Z\"]}], fMinHz <= First[#] <= fMaxHz &];\n  fr = keep[[All, 1]]; z = keep[[All, 2]];\n  Quiet @ Check[DCTKernel`SolveLadderGivenRs[0., fr, z, fr, z,\n      lambdaND, binsPerDecade, tauMinFactor, tauMaxFactor, weightPower], $Failed]];\n\n(* same file walk as the concentration fits (5.1): both directories, series letter each *)\nrsZeroRecs = Flatten[Table[\n  If[!StringQ[d[[1]]] || !DirectoryQ[d[[1]]], {},\n    Table[Module[{spec = rsZeroSpec[f]},\n      If[AssociationQ[spec] && TrueQ[spec[\"OK\"]],\n        <|\"Elec\" -> concTag[f, d[[2]]],\n          \"Conc\" -> N[concUM[f]], \"Spec\" -> spec|>, Nothing]],\n      {f, SortBy[FileNames[\"*.txt\", d[[1]]], {concElec[#], concUM[#]} &]}]],\n  {d, {{concentrationDir, seriesOfDir[concentrationDir]}, {concentrationDir2, seriesOfDir[concentrationDir2]}}}], 1];\n\n(* baseline spectra keyed the same way, so the two can be compared spectrum by spectrum.\n   N[] on the concentration in BOTH keys: getLabelUM returns an integer and concUM a real,\n   and 0 and 0. are different Association keys. *)\nbaseByKey   = Association[({StringTake[#File, 2], N@getLabelUM[#File]} -> #Spec) & /@ concGoodSpecs];\nrsZeroByKey = Association[({#Elec, N[#Conc]} -> #Spec) & /@ rsZeroRecs];\n\nrelZ[spec_] := Norm[spec[\"ZFit\"] - spec[\"ZData\"]]/Norm[spec[\"ZData\"]];\nslowK[spec_] := windowGeoMean[spec, Sequence @@ peakWindows[spec][[1]]];\nfastK[spec_] := windowGeoMean[spec, Sequence @@ peakWindows[spec][[2]]];\nfmtK[v_] := If[MissingQ[v], \"n/a\", NumberForm[v, {4, 1}]];\n\n(* fraction of the recovered capacitance sitting above the fit window's top rate (500 /s),\n   i.e. piled onto the fast edge of the tau grid. With Rs = 0 the missing series resistor\n   can only be mimicked by a very fast relaxation, so this is where it goes. *)\nedgeFrac[spec_] := Module[{tot = DCTPeakAnalysis`IntegrateSpectrum[spec]},\n  If[tot <= 0., 0., modeCap[spec, {500., Max[1./spec[\"Tau\"]]}]/tot]];\n\nrsZeroTable = Module[{keys},\n  keys = SortBy[Select[Keys[rsZeroByKey], First[#] === \"B1\" &], Last];\n  Grid[Prepend[\n    Table[Module[{b = baseByKey[k], z = rsZeroByKey[k]},\n      {NumberForm[Last[k], {4, 0}], NumberForm[b[\"Rs\"], {5, 1}],\n       NumberForm[100 relZ[b], {3, 2}], NumberForm[100 relZ[z], {3, 2}],\n       NumberForm[sensFF[b], {4, 3}], NumberForm[sensFF[z], {4, 3}],\n       fmtK[slowK[b]], fmtK[slowK[z]], fmtK[fastK[b]], fmtK[fastK[z]],\n       NumberForm[100 edgeFrac[z], {3, 1}]}], {k, keys}],\n    Style[#, Bold] & /@ {\"[Vanco]\\n(\\[Mu]M)\", \"Rs fitted\\n(\\[CapitalOmega])\", \"misfit %\\nbase\", \"misfit %\\nRs=0\",\n      \"ff\\nbase\", \"ff\\nRs=0\", \"slow \\[LeftAngleBracket]k\\[RightAngleBracket]\\nbase\", \"slow \\[LeftAngleBracket]k\\[RightAngleBracket]\\nRs=0\",\n      \"fast \\[LeftAngleBracket]k\\[RightAngleBracket]\\nbase\", \"fast \\[LeftAngleBracket]k\\[RightAngleBracket]\\nRs=0\", \"C above\\n500 /s (%)\"}],\n   Frame -> All, Alignment -> {{Right}}, Spacings -> {1.2, 0.5},\n   BaseStyle -> {FontFamily -> \"Arial\", FontSize -> 11}]];\n\nPrint[Style[\"Electrode B1, baseline vs Rs = 0\", Bold, 13]];\nPrint[rsZeroTable];\nPrint[Style[Row[{\"All \", Length[rsZeroRecs], \" spectra:  Rs fitted median \",\n  NumberForm[Median[#[\"Rs\"] & /@ Values[baseByKey]], {5, 1}], \" \\[CapitalOmega] (\",\n  NumberForm[Min[#[\"Rs\"] & /@ Values[baseByKey]], {5, 1}], \" to \",\n  NumberForm[Max[#[\"Rs\"] & /@ Values[baseByKey]], {5, 1}], \").   median |Z| misfit \",\n  NumberForm[100 Median[relZ /@ Values[baseByKey]], {3, 2}], \"% baseline vs \",\n  NumberForm[100 Median[relZ /@ Values[rsZeroByKey]], {3, 2}], \"% at Rs = 0.   median capacitance above 500 /s \",\n  NumberForm[100 Median[edgeFrac /@ Values[baseByKey]], {3, 1}], \"% baseline vs \",\n  NumberForm[100 Median[edgeFrac /@ Values[rsZeroByKey]], {3, 1}], \"% at Rs = 0.\"}], Italic]]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
       "data": "<div class=\"wl-print-output\"><div class=\"wl-print-line\"><div class=\"vscode-wolfram-wllatex-prerendered\" data-page-width-em=\"64\" data-latex-b64=\"XG1hdGhiZntcdGV4dHtFbGVjdHJvZGUgQjEsIGJhc2VsaW5lIHZzIFJzID0gMH19\"><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.8889em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">Electrode B1, baseline vs Rs = 0</span></span></span></span></span></span></div></div></div>",
       "mime": "x-application/wolfram-language-html"
      },
      {
       "data": "Print: [formula]",
       "mime": "text/plain"
      }
     ],
     "id": "2a4cdcf0-c010-45f7-b39b-031ea2c9a0be"
    },
    {
