     "id": "04f041ef-3a97-4e75-8f94-2d89a65c6e33"
    },
    {
     "items": [
      {
       "data": "<div class=\"wl-output-block\"><div class=\"wl-output-header\" style=\"display:flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;width:100%;min-height:22px;\" data-session-epoch=\"23243\" data-output-id=\"69\" data-out-n=\"645\" data-sub-idx=\"6\" data-output-format=\"SVG\" data-output-is-graphics=\"1\" data-cell-idx=\"124\" data-sub-start=\"18\" data-sub-end=\"33\"><span style=\"font-size:10px;color:#888;margin-right:8px;\">Out[645]=</span></div><div class=\"wl-output-content\"><span class=\"vscode-wolfram-gfx-marker\" style=\"display:none;\"></span><img class=\"vscode-wolfram-svg-output\" data-wl-img=\"c:\\\\Users\\\\Bob Lansdorp\\\\Documents\\\\DCT\\\\img\\\\EAB_DCT_analysis\\\\wl_17czs4zmp1c3f.svg\" width=\"747\" height=\"548\" src=\"img/EAB_DCT_analysis/wl_17czs4zmp1c3f.svg\"/></div></div>",
       "mime": "x-application/wolfram-language-html"
      },
      {
       "data": "(* output: graphics *)\n(* 8.3  Pooled folded fraction vs [vancomycin]: baseline against Rs = 0, all electrodes.\n   Curves are matched on concentration (not on position) so the difference column is\n   always like for like. *)\nrsFFCurve[recs_] := SortBy[KeyValueMap[{#1, Mean[#2]} &,\n  GroupBy[{N[#Conc], sensFF[#Spec]} & /@ recs, First -> Last]], First];\n\nbaseRecsAll   = <|\"Conc\" -> Last[#], \"Spec\" -> baseByKey[#]|> & /@ Keys[baseByKey];\nffBaseCurve   = rsFFCurve[baseRecsAll];\nffRsZeroCurve = rsFFCurve[rsZeroRecs];\n\nModule[{b = Association[Rule @@@ ffBaseCurve], z = Association[Rule @@@ ffRsZeroCurve], ks},\n  ks = Sort @ Intersection[Keys[b], Keys[z]];\n  Print[Grid[Prepend[\n     Table[{NumberForm[c, {4, 0}], NumberForm[b[c], {4, 3}], NumberForm[z[c], {4, 3}],\n            NumberForm[z[c] - b[c], {4, 3}]}, {c, ks}],\n     Style[#, Bold] & /@ {\"[Vanco] (\\[Mu]M)\", \"ff baseline\", \"ff Rs=0\", \"difference\"}],\n    Frame -> All, Alignment -> {{Right}}, Spacings -> {2, 0.6}]]];\n\nModule[{fg, bg, cMax},\n  fg = If[DCTPlots`$DCTTheme === \"Publication\", Black, White];\n  bg = If[DCTPlots`$DCTTheme === \"Publication\", White, GrayLevel[0.12]];\n  cMax = 1.03 Max[ffBaseCurve[[All, 1]]];\n  ListLinePlot[{ffBaseCurve, ffRsZeroCurve}, Joined -> True, PlotMarkers -> {Automatic, 9},\n    PlotStyle -> {Directive[RGBColor[0.20, 0.45, 0.85], AbsoluteThickness[1.8]],\n                  Directive[RGBColor[0.85, 0.25, 0.20], AbsoluteThickness[1.8], Dashed]},\n    PlotTheme -> \"Default\", Frame -> True, Axes -> False, Background -> bg,\n    FrameStyle -> Directive[fg, AbsoluteThickness[1.1]],\n    FrameTicks -> {{DCTPlots`ThemeLinTicks[0., 1., fg], None}, {DCTPlots`ThemeLinTicks[0., cMax, fg], None}},\n    FrameTicksStyle -> Directive[fg, 12], LabelStyle -> Directive[fg, 13, FontFamily -> \"Arial\"],\n    FrameLabel -> {Style[\"[Vancomycin] (\\[Mu]M)\", 14, fg], Style[\"Fraction folded\", 14, fg]},\n    PlotRange -> {{0, cMax}, {0, 1}}, PlotRangePadding -> {Scaled[0.03], None},\n    PlotLegends -> Placed[LineLegend[{RGBColor[0.20, 0.45, 0.85], RGBColor[0.85, 0.25, 0.20]},\n      {\"baseline (Rs fitted)\", \"Rs = 0\"}, LabelStyle -> Directive[fg, 12]], {0.72, 0.35}],\n    ImageSize -> 560, AspectRatio -> 0.7]]",
       "mime": "text/plain"
      }
     ],
     "id": "d658d89a-6a34-4f63-80af-8e824ac23de7"
    }
   ],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## 9. A resistor in parallel with the ladder instead of in series\nSection 8 removed the series resistance. This section moves it: the resistor now sits in parallel with the Maxwell ladder, so the interfacial admittance gains a real, frequency-independent term,\n\nY(w) = Gp + i w C0 + D * Sum_k g_k * i w / (1 + i w tau_k),   Z = 1/Y,\n\nwith Gp = 1/Rp >= 0 solved for alongside C0 and g by the same non-negative least squares. Physically a series R is the electrolyte between the reference and the working electrode, while a parallel R is a DC leakage or non-saturating faradaic path across the monolayer. The two have opposite frequency signatures, so neither can stand in for the other.\n\nThe solve is written out here instead of taken from `DCTKernel`, which has no parallel column. Everything else is the baseline: same tau grid, same second-difference regularisation on g only (C0 and Gp are unpenalised), same |Y|^p weighting, same non-negativity.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### 9.1 The solve, and a consistency check\n`parallelFit[file, rs]` adds the Gp column and returns the same keys as the packaged solve. Called with rs at the baseline's fitted value it becomes the baseline model plus an optional leakage path, which is also a check on this reimplementation: if the data want no leakage then Gp should go to zero and every number should reproduce the packaged fit.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* 9.1  Maxwell ladder with a parallel conductance Gp:  Y = Gp + i w C0 + K.g,  Z = rs + 1/Y.\n   rs is FIXED, not optimised: rs = 0 is the parallel-only model of 9.2, rs = the baseline's\n   fitted value is the baseline model plus an optional leakage path (9.1). Column order is\n   [Gp | C0 | g...]; the second-difference matrix gets two zero columns so only g is\n   smoothed; lambda is scaled by the median column norm of the g block, as in DCTKernel. *)\nparallelFit[file_, rs_] := Module[\n  {dat, keep, fr, z, om, y, w, tau, n, dlog, kmat, kuse, aMat, aW, bW, aRI, bRI,\n   d2, dFull, aCols, lam, aAug, bAug, x, gp, c0, g, yFit},\n  dat = DCTDataImport`ImportEIS[file];\n  If[FailureQ[dat], Return[$Failed]];\n  keep = Select[Transpose[{dat[\"FreqHz\"], dat[\"Z\"]}], fMinHz <= First[#] <= fMaxHz &];\n  fr = keep[[All, 1]]; z = keep[[All, 2]];\n  om = 2. Pi fr; y = 1./(z - rs); w = Abs[y]^weightPower;\n  tau = DCTKernel`BuildTauGrid[fr, binsPerDecade, tauMinFactor, tauMaxFactor];\n  n = Length[tau]; dlog = 1./binsPerDecade;\n  kmat = Table[(I om[[j]])/(1 + I om[[j]] tau[[k]]), {j, Length[om]}, {k, n}];\n  kuse = dlog kmat;\n  (* [Gp column of 1s | C0 column of i*omega | ladder] *)\n  aMat = Join[Transpose[{ConstantArray[1., Length[om]]}], Transpose[{I om}], kuse, 2];\n  aW = DiagonalMatrix[Sqrt[w]] . aMat; bW = Sqrt[w] y;\n  aRI = Join[Re[aW], Im[aW]]; bRI = Join[Re[bW], Im[bW]];\n  d2 = DCTKernel`SecondDifferenceMatrix[n];\n  dFull = ArrayFlatten[{{ConstantArray[0., {n - 2, 2}], d2}}];\n  aCols = aRI[[All, 3 ;;]];\n  lam = lambdaND Median[Total[aCols^2, {1}]];\n  aAug = Join[aRI, Sqrt[lam] N[Normal[dFull]], 1];\n  bAug = Join[bRI, ConstantArray[0., n - 2]];\n  x = Quiet @ Check[NNLSFit`NNLS[aAug, bAug], $Failed];\n  If[x === $Failed || !VectorQ[x, NumericQ] || Length[x] =!= n + 2, Return[$Failed]];\n  gp = x[[1]]; c0 = x[[2]]; g = x[[3 ;;]];\n  yFit = gp + (I om) c0 + kuse . g;\n  <|\"OK\" -> True, \"Rs\" -> rs, \"Gp\" -> gp, \"Tau\" -> tau, \"g\" -> g, \"C0\" -> c0,\n    \"FreqHz\" -> fr, \"ZData\" -> z, \"ZFit\" -> rs + 1./yFit, \"YIntData\" -> y, \"YIntFit\" -> yFit|>];\n\n(* locate the raw file behind an electrode tag such as \"B1\": the letter picks the\n   directory, the digit picks the electrode inside it *)\nconcFileOf[tag_, um_] := Module[{dir, n},\n  dir = If[StringTake[tag, 1] === seriesOfDir[concentrationDir2], concentrationDir2, concentrationDir];\n  n   = StringDrop[tag, 1];\n  First @ Select[FileNames[\"*.txt\", dir], concElec[#] == n && concUM[#] == um &]];\n\n(* consistency check: baseline Rs, leakage path allowed *)\nleakCheck = Table[Module[{k = {\"B1\", c}, b = baseByKey[{\"B1\", c}], s},\n    s = parallelFit[concFileOf[\"B1\", c], baseByKey[{\"B1\", c}][\"Rs\"]];\n    {NumberForm[c, {4, 0}], If[s[\"Gp\"] == 0., \"0 (exactly)\", ScientificForm[s[\"Gp\"], 3]],\n     NumberForm[1*^9 s[\"C0\"], {5, 1}], NumberForm[1*^9 b[\"C0\"], {5, 1}],\n     NumberForm[sensFF[s], {4, 3}], NumberForm[sensFF[b], {4, 3}],\n     ScientificForm[Max[Abs[s[\"g\"] - b[\"g\"]]], 2]}],\n  {c, Sort[N@getLabelUM[#] & /@ Select[concGoodSpecs, StringStartsQ[#File, \"B1 \"] &][[All, \"File\"]]]}];\n\nPrint[Style[\"Baseline Rs, leakage path allowed: does the fit want one?\", Bold, 13]];\nPrint[Grid[Prepend[leakCheck,\n   Style[#, Bold] & /@ {\"[Vanco] (\\[Mu]M)\", \"Gp fitted (S)\", \"C0 here (nF)\", \"C0 packaged (nF)\",\n     \"ff here\", \"ff packaged\", \"max |dg| (F/dec)\"}],\n  Frame -> All, Alignment -> {{Right}}, Spacings -> {1.6, 0.6},\n  BaseStyle -> {FontFamily -> \"Arial\", FontSize -> 11}]]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
